    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `customerCode` is computed deterministically as `<REGION>-<HASH8>` in the `assignCustomerCode` step of the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline, which runs inside the create transaction *before* the owner is saved. I added collision de-duplication in two small pieces, each where it belongs:\n\n**1. `util/CustomerCode.java`** \u2014 added a reusable pure helper, since this class already owns the code format and the `-` separator:\n\n```java\npublic static String deduplicate(String customerCode, Set<String> taken) {\n    if (!taken.contains(customerCode)) {\n        return customerCode;\n    }\n    for (int n = 2; ; n++) {\n        String candidate = customerCode + SEPARATOR + n;\n        if (!taken.contains(candidate)) {\n            return candidate;\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nReturns the base code unchanged when it's free, otherwise appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that isn't already taken.\n\n**2. `rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the pipeline step now collects the codes already held by existing owners and de-duplicates against them:\n\n```java\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {\n    String region = OwnerRegion.of(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity());\n    String code = CustomerCode.of(region, owner.getTelephone(), owner.getLastName());\n    Set<String> taken = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()\n            .map(Owner::getCustomerCode)\n            .filter(Objects::nonNull)\n            .collect(Collectors.toSet());\n    owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCode.deduplicate(code, taken));\n}\n```\n\nThis follows the same in-transaction, \"read `findAll()` before save so the new owner isn't matched against itself\" pattern used by sibling steps like `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` and `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`. Downstream derivations still work: `CustomerCode.region(...)` splits on the *first* `-`, so a deduped `NSW-1A2B3C4D-2` still yields locality `NSW`.\n\nThe `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test passes \u2014 its guarantee (distinct owners get distinct codes) holds, and the dedup rule now backs it even in the rare hash-collision case that can't be forced black-box.",
